Scoring formula b3.v7, reworked for Verification Coverage (docs/proposals/coverage.md, 念誠 11/19)

Replaces loop/proposals/scoring-b3v7.patch. The loop guard (scripts/loop_guard.py) keeps a session from editing
pickfit/score.py, pickfit/schema.py and schema/, so the change is proposed here. It also carries the unprotected files
that only work with it (pickfit/extract.py's R4 part, pickfit/cli.py's score flags, pickfit/discover/store.py's
ReadOnlyPipelineDB, the backfill, comparison and recompute scripts, and the tests). It applies LAST, after
security-schema.patch, video-captions.patch and tokens-t5-2-cli-judge-text-only.patch (loop/proposals/APPLY.md), on
top of pickfit/coverage.py, which is on the branch already; schema/software.v1.json in it is scripts/export_schema.py's
output with all four applied.

Kept from b3.v7:
- R1, R10: scores.inputs keeps the raw GitHub signals and issues; maintenance, hygiene and responsiveness are computed
  from them; refresh_scores recomputes every part with no call; earlier formulas' results go to scores.history;
  scripts/migrate_score_inputs.py backfills inputs from runs/pipeline.db.
- R2, R3: DocsRubric keeps prompt_version, input_sha, renderer_version and grader, and is reused by its raw text
  (--regrade-before, --regrade-model); scripts/compare_rubric.py (paid, plans only without --run).
- R4: extract.RUBRIC_IN_EXTRACTION (off).
- R8: "other" and the five subject categories use the pooled popularity refs "_all", not dev_cli's.

Changed against b3.v7:
- R5 reads the new security contract (security.assessment.level: known findings only; coverage apart). An unknown
  never deducts, caps or blocks. What known findings do is a set of settings whose defaults are today's rules:
  schema.SECURITY_CAP_LEVELS (default blocked, exposed, conditional: where sec.v2's status is vulnerable, so the 79
  cap is the same), schema.SECURITY_NO_TREASURE_LEVELS (default none), score.SECURITY_EXPOSED_DEDUCTION (0) and
  score.STALE_FIX_PENALTY (0). quality.raw_total and quality.security record what applied.
- R6 (pull thin data toward the category mean) and R7 (the run's depth in sandbox_verification) are out of the
  quality score: they are Verification Coverage's (pickfit/coverage.py: reliability, depth). QUALITY_PRIORS,
  SANDBOX_DEPTH and scripts/calibrate_quality_priors.py are gone.
- quality.confidence is derived from the coverage (coverage.quality_confidence): the same number as before for
  every record in data/software; the security dimension is never in it.
- The treasure and cap rules are settings, today's rules by default: schema.UNCHECKED_CAN_BE_TREASURE (True, R9),
  schema.UNVERIFIED_CAP (True: the 69 cap), schema.TREASURE_MIN_SECURITY_COVERAGE and TREASURE_MIN_FUNCTION_COVERAGE
  (None). treasure.blocked_by names the rule that kept a record from being a treasure. `pickfit coverage rules`
  compares the candidates (docs/proposals/coverage-distribution.md). If a coverage threshold is switched on, its
  measure comes from pickfit/coverage.py, which the loop may edit: add it to scripts/loop_guard.py's PROTECTED then.

With the default settings, over data/software: no quality total, confidence, cap or treasure changes. Formulas move
b3.v6 -> b3.v7 (and +visual.v1), scores gain inputs (legacy components), history, raw_total and quality.security, and
124 records of "other" and the subject categories get a new popularity (R8, -1.3 to +0.7; none crosses into or out of
treasure).

    git apply --check loop/proposals/coverage-scoring-b3v7.patch
    git apply loop/proposals/coverage-scoring-b3v7.patch
    uv run python scripts/export_schema.py --check
    uv run pytest

